what's going on everybody it's warren  welcome back to the cosmic wonder where  we talk all things marvel and mcu and  right off the bat spoiler warning if you  have not seen spider-man no way home we  are about to dive into some spoilers for  that film so you should click away now  if you are still with me i had to kind  of lie about the title and put rumor in  the title so i didn't spoil it for those  who haven't seen no way home but tom  holland has finally addressed he has  finally talked about the other two  in spider-man no way home and what it  was like to work with them after going  all of this time and everybody denying  that they are all three in spider-man  knowing home andrew garfield saying that  he's not the werewolf toby pretty much  staying quiet about everything and tom  doing his absolute best to not spoil  everything and he didn't all for us to  get that epic moment on screen that we  saw where we saw andrew garfield and  then toby maguire show up after finally  experiencing that in an interview on  marvel's website directly we have  zendaya and tom holland talking about  what it was like to have andrew garfield  and toby mcguire on the set so let's  check out what tom and zendaya had to  say about working with the other two  spider-man and of course if you're new  to the channel be sure to subscribe so  you can stay up to date on all of the  latest mcu news so like i said this is  coming directly from marvel's website  and the article is titled spider-man no  way home tom holland and zendaya on new  and returning surprise characters now if  i wasn't so sick still and it wasn't so  hard to talk i would go over all of  these but i'm just gonna go over a few  and let's start with charlie cox because  that was an awesome surprise even though  some of us knew it was coming it was  still insanely exciting to see on screen  it starts off by saying does that suit  cane and glasses combination look  familiar yes charlie cox is once again  playing matt murdock making a surprise  appearance to offer peter mae parker and  happy legal advice and he's a very good  lawyer tom holland said we had so much  fun working with charlie it's really  interesting doing a scene between two  superheroes that has no real superhero  stuff in it apart from the bit when he  catches the brick it was awesome zendaya  then says i didn't get to be there in  which tom holland said you weren't there  for that oh you were there for that in  which zendaya said i was there for the  behind the scenes watching you guys but  i didn't get to be in it and tom holland  said but it was great i loved working  with charlie now like i said i'm not  going to go over all of these but i do  want to talk about what tom had to say  about willem dafoe because i think he  just absolutely crushed his character  returning after years and years and  years of playing the green goblin he  came back and absolutely killed the role  it says if that cackle sends a chill  down your spine you're not alone  returning as norman osborne slash the  green goblin defoe is downright  terrifying though peter does think he  kind of looks like a green elf at first  tom holland says i've never worked with  an actor who was able to give a director  so many options he has this one speech  in the film where he's talking about  peter's kind of existential crisis and  he and then zendaya cut him off and said  scared the hell out of everyone to be  honest tom then said he must have done  that scene 30 times and they were all  different in which zendaya said the  coolest thing is that everyone's so  lovely and then they just play these  very evil characters he's so good at  just like being lovely you know hey how  are you and then green goblin like whoa  and now here's what tom holland ins and  dey had to say about working with tobey  maguire and andrew garfield it says last  seen on screen as spider-man in 2007  mcguire's version of the character  enters this multiverse to help out  holland's peter now older and wiser he  serves as a spidey mentor of sorts to  the young hero tom holland toby was so  funny zendaya he was so cool tom holland  says we have so many little inside jokes  that came up from working with toby  definitely not your dad he says and  that's a quote and i'm assuming an  inside joke zendaya then says t mcgee in  which tom holland also says t mcgee man  he was so funny he was really excited to  be back you could tell it really meant a  lot to him him putting the suit on again  us getting back together it was awesome  zendaya says that first day i was so  nervous for you in which tom says yeah i  was stressed zendaya said we had to do a  rehearsal and me and jacob felt like  your parents tom jokes and says dropping  me off at school zendaya says like  dropping you off at kindergarten for the  first day like i hope the other kids  like him and like i hope he doesn't come  back crying and so we were just there  and i was taking pictures of you guys so  that you could have it it was so cute  tom then says you do have some amazing  pictures of us zendaya i do i do but  yeah he was so lovely and hilarious  unintentionally sometimes and tom's  final words were he's hilarious and i'm  hoping at least one point in time on set  behind the scenes there is a video or  picture somewhere out there of all three  spider-man or at least toby and tom  doing the emo parker dance  now i just love what they said about  toby about how excited he was to be back  and that it really meant a lot to him to  be back because he's my spider-man he's  the spider-man that i grew up with he's  the one that i'll always have the  biggest emotional attachment to and the  fact that he was excited to return and  it meant a lot to him means a lot to me  and i'm sure many other people out there  as well and i personally really loved  that he played the older type of mentor  type to peter parker to not just our  peter parker but to andrew as well he  has that scene with andrew where he  tells him you know don't give up on love  it was hard for me and mj but we made it  work and i do love the role that andrew  garfield got to play and what it meant  to him and here's what tom and zendaya  had to say about working with andrew it  says last seen on screen as spider-man  in 2014 garfield returns to the  character to once again crawl up the  walls alongside maguire's version of the  character garfield works to help  holland's peter with the challenges he's  currently facing tom holland says andrew  garfield the legend himself he's such a  lovely guy i think this film was his way  of making peace with spider-man it was  such a privilege to work with him i know  that it meant a lot to him then zendaya  says some really touching words here she  says it was so beautiful to see toby  andrew and tom care so deeply about the  characters and what their characters  what their journey had been as  spider-man it was so beautiful to see  all of you guys connect on that and be  able to talk to each other about such a  special experience that very few people  have been able to don the suit it was so  great to see how much you guys all  really cared and had each other's back  it was really sweet in which tom holland  replied it's like a brotherhood now i  personally really love this and i  actually have to agree with what tom  holland said here it does feel like this  was sort of a redemption moment for  andrew garfield you know the amazing  spider-man movies get a lot of hate and  that's not andrew's fault i actually  think he's a fantastic spider-man but  this film spider-man no way home he  really shined especially for me i think  that he did an incredible job and he was  my favorite part of the movie one of  them at least every time we talked about  gwen and when he talked about not  holding back his punches anymore got me  choked up and when he caught mj that was  such a perfect scene in such a  redemption moment for him i cried all of  the times when i watched this movie  during this part and then you have the  scene where he's talking to toby and  toby's like wait a second you're amazing  you're amazing and he says not gonna lie  i needed to hear that you can tell that  this is really about andrew and his  films it's two part right because he's  the amazing spider-man toby is saying  you're amazing but also you have to  imagine that andrew felt kind of bad  about how fans reacted to the films and  this is toby saying no you're amazing  you're an amazing spider-man and i think  that was overall just an insanely cool  scene and i look forward to getting to  know more about what happened behind the  scenes i look forward to the behind the  scenes videos where we see all of them  interacting together no doubt they'll  release those over time i mean this was  kind of secretly released on marvel's  website it wasn't advertised that much  because obviously marvel and sony are  still trying to keep the other  spider-man a secret but of course it'll  all come out probably pretty soon but in  the meantime let me know what you think  about this in the comments down below  and what was your favorite part of  spiderman no way home don't forget to  like the video and subscribe and hit  that notification bell so you don't miss  out on any of the latest videos and of  course for live updates you can follow  me on instagram and twitter and as  always thank you all so much for  watching woof  you

